Source: @PKG@
Section: database
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Docker Hardened Images <dhi@docker.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13),
 libbz2-dev,
 libcurl4-openssl-dev,
 liblz4-dev,
 libsnappy-dev,
 libssl-dev,
 libzstd-dev,
 pkg-config,
 tcl,
 uuid-dev,
 zlib1g-dev
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Homepage: https://docs.keydb.dev

Package: @PKG@-tools
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Provides: keydb-tools
Conflicts: keydb-tools
Replaces: keydb-tools
Description: KeyDB command-line interface and utilities
 KeyDB is a multithreaded fork of Redis that speaks the RESP protocol and is
 configuration-compatible with Redis, adding active replication, multi-master
 and FLASH (RocksDB-backed) storage.
 .
 This package provides the client-side tools keydb-cli, keydb-benchmark and
 keydb-diagnostic-tool.

Package: @PKG@-server
Architecture: any
Depends: @PKG@-tools (= ${binary:Version}), ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Provides: keydb-server, keydb
Conflicts: keydb-server
Replaces: keydb-server
Description: KeyDB server (multithreaded RESP-compatible key/value datastore)
 KeyDB is a multithreaded fork of Redis that speaks the RESP protocol and is
 configuration-compatible with Redis, adding active replication, multi-master
 and FLASH (RocksDB-backed) storage.
 .
 This package provides keydb-server built with TLS and FLASH support, the
 keydb-check-rdb / keydb-check-aof helpers and the default configuration file
 /etc/keydb/keydb.conf.

Package: @PKG@-sentinel
Architecture: any
Depends: @PKG@-server (= ${binary:Version}), ${misc:Depends}
Provides: keydb-sentinel
Conflicts: keydb-sentinel
Replaces: keydb-sentinel
Description: KeyDB sentinel high-availability monitor
 KeyDB is a multithreaded fork of Redis that speaks the RESP protocol and is
 configuration-compatible with Redis, adding active replication, multi-master
 and FLASH (RocksDB-backed) storage.
 .
 This package provides keydb-sentinel (the failover monitor) and the default
 configuration file /etc/keydb/sentinel.conf.
